The candidates ride with the beacon

Run 566's panel had neither the number of candidates nor the class of them,
though the marks were written.  The panel is a scrolling window: a mark
written once is gone by the time the console text catches up with it.  The
beacon is written every fourth mark and is never covered -- the waypoints
w8m3 have been on the screen through every round since.

So the numbers ride with it.  The matching writes them into three globals
and the beacon prints them: c is the number of candidates the matching was
given, r why the last one was turned away (0 is none, 1 a notifier, 2
something that is not a dictionary), and f the class of that candidate.

The marks that are written once stay as they are -- they are still worth
having when the screen holds them.

diff --git a/osfmk/kern/startup.c b/osfmk/kern/startup.c
index 3fa75ef..a3b6916 100644
--- a/osfmk/kern/startup.c
+++ b/osfmk/kern/startup.c
@@ -491,6 +491,23 @@ nio_dc_putu(unsigned long v)
 volatile int nio_boot_waypoint = 0;
 volatile int nio_match_waypoint = 0;
 
+/* nio: what the matching was given, and what it did with it.
+ *
+ * A mark on the panel is only worth what survives the scrolling.
+ * Run 566 wrote the number of candidates and the class of each
+ * of them, and the panel had none of them left: the console text
+ * that keeps coming went over them.  The beacon is written
+ * every fourth mark and is never covered, so the numbers ride
+ * with it.
+ *
+ * c is the number of candidates the matching was given, r why the
+ * last one was turned away (0 is none, 1 a notifier, 2 something
+ * that is not a dictionary) and f the class of that candidate.
+ */
+volatile unsigned int nio_cand_count = 0;
+volatile unsigned int nio_cand_reason = 0;
+char nio_cand_class[32] = "?";
+
 /* nio: a beacon that never sleeps.  The heartbeat thread below uses delay(),
  * which needs working timers; it prints HB 1 and stops, and that tells us
  * nothing about whether the kernel is alive.  This one spins on its own and
@@ -517,6 +534,12 @@ nio_beacon_thread(void *arg, wait_result_t wr)
 				nio_dc_putu((unsigned)nio_boot_waypoint);
 				nio_dc_puts("m");
 				nio_dc_putu((unsigned)nio_match_waypoint);
+				nio_dc_puts("c");
+				nio_dc_putu(nio_cand_count);
+				nio_dc_puts("r");
+				nio_dc_putu(nio_cand_reason);
+				nio_dc_puts(" ");
+				nio_dc_puts(nio_cand_class);
 				nio_dc_puts(" ");
 			}
 		}
